N5008 [temp.inst]/1: an alias declaration does not require a complete type,
so `using str = basic_str<char>;' (an alias TEMPLATE naming a class template
specialization whose argument is still incomplete) must not instantiate it.
The typedef branch of convert_non_template_declaration cleared
skip_typechecking_elaborate instead of restoring it when the alias template's
own declaration was converted underneath, so the outer resolver elaborated
the class (libstdc++ 11 pmr::string: "dropped 4 system-header declarations";
here: `a' never constructed, assertion 1 failed).
